# What the dev watcher must not watch.
#
# Tauri rebuilds the app when anything under `src-tauri/` changes, and the
# vendored agent writes *runtime state into its own install directory* — a
# `.mcode-active/<pid>.json` claim file per session, and more beside it. Every
# one of those reads as a source change, so the app rebuilt itself in a loop
# while a session was running: `File resources/mcode/.mcode-active/… changed.
# Rebuilding application…` on a timer, with the window reloading under the
# reader.
#
# Ignored whole, and that is safe because nothing here is source this app
# compiles: it is the CLI and the runtime it ships with, staged by
# `scripts/vendor-mcode.sh` and copied into a release bundle as-is.

resources/mcode
